---
import Closing from "../components/sections/Closing.astro";

import Layout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import Intro from "../components/Intro.astro";
import Chapter from "../components/Chapter.astro";
import Faq from "../components/Faq.astro";
---

<Layout title="Financial coaching services" active="services">
  <Intro
    eyebrow={"FINANCIAL COACHING"}
    description={
      "Explore where personalized coaching can help: your everyday budget, your debt, and the goals you want to move toward."
    }
  >
    <Fragment slot="title">
      Make your money
      <br /> <em>work for your life.</em>
    </Fragment>
  </Intro>
  <Chapter label={"01 / PERSONALIZED BUDGETING"}>
    <Fragment slot="title">
      A budget you can
      <br /> come back to.
    </Fragment>
    <p class="lead">A useful budget starts with the life you actually live.</p>
    <p>
      Bring your income, regular commitments, and changing expenses into one
      clearer picture. The goal is a practical plan you can use when everyday
      decisions come up.
    </p>
    <h3>This may be your starting point if…</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>You’re not sure where your money goes each month.</li>
      <li>You have a budget, but it rarely matches real life.</li>
      <li>
        You want to make room for saving without guessing what’s available.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <a class="text-link" href="/contact/?goal=budget">
      Talk about your budget
    </a>
  </Chapter>
  <Chapter label={"02 / DEBT PAYOFF PLANNING"}>
    <Fragment slot="title">
      Turn a list of balances
      <br /> into a direction.
    </Fragment>
    <p class="lead">Debt feels different when you can see a next step.</p>
    <p>
      Explore a payoff plan in the context of your other responsibilities and
      goals. Personalized guidance can help you think through priorities and
      what is realistic for your situation.
    </p>
    <h3>Start with the questions that matter.</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Which balances are taking up the most attention?</li>
      <li>What can your budget support consistently?</li>
      <li>How does paying down debt fit with your other priorities?</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You don’t need to send statements or account numbers to introduce
      yourself.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/contact/?goal=debt">
      Discuss a debt payoff plan
    </a>
  </Chapter>
  <Chapter label={"03 / FINANCIAL GOALS"}>
    <Fragment slot="title">
      Give your goals
      <br /> a place in the plan.
    </Fragment>
    <p class="lead">
      Big ambitions become more useful when they connect to everyday choices.
    </p>
    <p>
      Whether you’re preparing for a change, building savings, or looking for
      more financial stability, coaching starts by understanding what progress
      means to you.
    </p>
    <h3>A useful goal has context.</h3>
    <p>
      Consider what you’re working toward, why it matters, and when you would
      like to get there. Those details help shape a conversation about practical
      next steps.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/contact/?goal=goals">
      Share what you’re working toward
    </a>
  </Chapter>
  <Chapter label={"WHO IT’S FOR"}>
    <Fragment slot="title">
      Different lives.
      <br /> Personal guidance.
    </Fragment>
    <div class="reading-cards">
      <article>
        <h3>Individuals</h3>
        <p>
          Find a starting point for your own budget, debt, or goals—even if
          you’ve never worked with a coach.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Couples</h3>
        <p>
          Bring shared priorities and different perspectives into a conversation
          about what you want your money to support.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Small-business owners</h3>
        <p>
          Describe the budgeting and financial planning challenges of running
          your business. Discuss the right scope of coaching directly with Matt.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </Chapter>
  <Faq
    items={[
      [
        "Do I need to choose one service?",
        "No. You can select several interests in the intake form, or choose “Finding a starting point.” Your priorities can overlap.",
      ],
      [
        "What does coaching cost?",
        "Discuss fees and the scope of work directly with Matt before getting started. The site does not list a fixed package or price.",
      ],
      [
        "What if my situation doesn’t fit these examples?",
        "Use the introduction form to describe what you need. The first conversation is a chance to explore whether Afin is a fit.",
      ],
    ]}
  />
  <Closing />
</Layout>
